WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.510
Utqiaġvik, Alaska, in the Arctic tundra.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.390
Its February mean is minus
24.4 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.350
Dodge City, Kansas, on the Great Plains.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.790
Winters are cold here too: January
averages 0.6 degrees Celsius.

5
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.570
Neither has forest.

6
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.650
Tundra grows mosses, sedges and lichens.

7
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.390
The prairie grows grass.

8
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.870
On the tall-grass steppes,
the soil is chernozem.

9
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.470
It covers about 230
million hectares worldwide,

10
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.070
growing wheat, barley and maize.

11
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.890
So why is only one soil so fertile?

12
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.010
More rain?

13
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.010
Richer rock?

14
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.950
In this mission, you'll
compare the two climates,

15
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.370
month by month, on the same axes.

16
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.430
Then you'll dig into each soil,
and link it to the climate above.

17
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.530
Your mission: explain why
grassland soil is so fertile,

18
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.160
while tundra soil is not.
